<p><b>May 1</b>
</p>
<div id=3D"mp-tfa-img" style=3D"float: left; margin: 0.5em 0.9em 0.4em 0em;=
">
<div class=3D"thumbinner mp-thumb" style=3D"background: transparent; color:=
 inherit; border: none; padding: 0; max-width: 142px;">
<span typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Coun=
cilofClermont.jpg" class=3D"mw-file-description" title=3D"Pope Urban II's c=
all for the First Crusade at the Council of Clermont"><img alt=3D"Pope Urba=
n II's call for the First Crusade at the Council of Clermont" src=3D"https:=
//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/CouncilofClermont.jpg/2=
50px-CouncilofClermont.jpg" decoding=3D"async" width=3D"142" height=3D"137"=
 class=3D"mw-file-element" data-file-width=3D"1072" data-file-height=3D"103=
5"></a></span><div class=3D"thumbcaption" style=3D"padding: 0.25em 0; word-=
wrap: break-word;"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Urban_II" =
title=3D"Pope Urban II">Pope Urban II</a>'s call for the <a href=3D"https:/=
/en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Crusade" title=3D"First Crusade">First Crusade=
</a> at the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Council_of_Clermont" t=
itle=3D"Council of Clermont">Council of Clermont</a></div></div></div>
<p>The <b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crusading_movement" titl=
e=3D"Crusading movement">Crusading movement</a></b> was a major religious, =
political, and military endeavour of the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.or=
g/wiki/Middle_Ages" title=3D"Middle Ages">Middle Ages</a>, usually dated fr=
om the 1095 <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Council_of_Clermont" t=
itle=3D"Council of Clermont">Council of Clermont</a>. There <a href=3D"http=
s://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Urban_II" title=3D"Pope Urban II">Pope Urban=
&#160;II</a> proclaimed the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_=
Crusade" title=3D"First Crusade">First Crusade</a> in support of <a href=3D=
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eastern_Christianity" title=3D"Eastern Chris=
tianity">Eastern Christians</a> under Muslim rule, framing it as a form of =
penitential <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_pilgrimage" =
title=3D"Christian pilgrimage">pilgrimage</a>. The crusaders founded <a hre=
f=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crusader_states" title=3D"Crusader state=
s">four states</a> in the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Levant" =
title=3D"Levant">Levant</a>, the defence of which inspired further <a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crusades" title=3D"Crusades">Crusades</a>=
. The <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope" title=3D"Pope">papacy<=
/a> later launched campaigns against Muslims in <a href=3D"https://en.wikip=
edia.org/wiki/Iberian_Peninsula" title=3D"Iberian Peninsula">Iberia</a>, <a=
 href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paganism" title=3D"Paganism">pagans<=
/a> in the Baltic, and other opponents of its authority. Core crusading for=
ces were heavily armed <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knight" tit=
le=3D"Knight">knights</a>, backed by infantry, local troops, and naval aid =
from maritime cities. These papal-sanctioned wars fostered distinctive inst=
itutions and ideologies. Funding was initially improvised, but later suppor=
ted via <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Papal_income_tax" title=3D=
"Papal income tax">papal taxes on clergy</a> and the sale of <a href=3D"htt=
ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crusade_indulgence" title=3D"Crusade indulgence"=
>indulgences</a>. The fusion of chivalric and monastic ideals led to the ri=
se of <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military_order_(religious_so=
ciety)" title=3D"Military order (religious society)">military orders</a>. T=
he movement extended <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Chris=
tianity" title=3D"Western Christianity">Western Christendom</a> and left la=
sting marks on art and literature. <i>(<b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.o=
rg/wiki/Crusading_movement" title=3D"Crusading movement">Full&#160;article.=
..</a></b>)</i>
</p>
