<p>The <b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuji-class_battleship" t=
itle=3D"Fuji-class battleship"><i>Fuji</i> class</a></b> was a two-ship <a =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ship_class" title=3D"Ship class">clas=
s</a> of <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pre-dreadnought_battleshi=
p" title=3D"Pre-dreadnought battleship">pre-dreadnought battleships</a> bui=
lt for the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imperial_Japanese_Navy"=
 title=3D"Imperial Japanese Navy">Imperial Japanese Navy</a> (IJN) in the m=
id-1890s. They were the first battleships in the IJN, and were constructed =
in the United Kingdom as Japan lacked the industrial facilities needed to b=
uild them. The ships participated in the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.or=
g/wiki/Russo-Japanese_War" title=3D"Russo-Japanese War">Russo-Japanese War<=
/a> of 1904=E2=80=931905, including the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org=
/wiki/Battle_of_Port_Arthur" title=3D"Battle of Port Arthur">Battle of Port=
 Arthur</a> in February 1904 and two bombardments of <a href=3D"https://en.=
wikipedia.org/wiki/L%C3%BCshunkou" title=3D"L=C3=BCshunkou">Port Arthur</a>=
 the following month. <i><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_=
battleship_Yashima" title=3D"Japanese battleship Yashima">Yashima</a></i> s=
truck a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naval_mine" title=3D"Naval=
 mine">mine</a> off Port Arthur in May and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.=
org/wiki/Capsizing" title=3D"Capsizing">capsized</a> while under tow severa=
l hours later. <i><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_battles=
hip_Fuji" title=3D"Japanese battleship Fuji">Fuji</a></i> <i>(pictured)</i>=
 fought in the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_the_Yello=
w_Sea" title=3D"Battle of the Yellow Sea">Battle of the Yellow Sea</a> and =
the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Tsushima" title=3D"B=
attle of Tsushima">Battle of Tsushima</a>, and was lightly damaged in the l=
atter action. She was reclassified as a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org=
/wiki/Coastal_defence_ship" title=3D"Coastal defence ship">coast defence sh=
ip</a> in 1910 and served as a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tra=
ining_ship" title=3D"Training ship">training ship</a> for the rest of her a=
ctive career. <i>Fuji</i> was <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hulk=
_(ship_type)" title=3D"Hulk (ship type)">hulked</a> in 1922, converted into=
 a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barracks_ship" title=3D"Barrack=
s ship">barracks ship</a> fitted with classrooms, and was finally <a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ship_breaking" title=3D"Ship breaking">br=
oken up</a> for scrap in 1948. <i>(<b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w=
iki/Fuji-class_battleship" title=3D"Fuji-class battleship">This&#160;articl=
e</a></b> is part of a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:F=
eatured_topics" title=3D"Wikipedia:Featured topics">featured topic</a>: <b>=
<a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Featured_topics/Battlesh=
ips_of_Japan" title=3D"Wikipedia:Featured topics/Battleships of Japan"><i>B=
attleships of Japan</i></a></b>.)</i>
</p>
