<p><b>May 4</b>
</p>
<div id=3D"mp-tfa-img" style=3D"float: left; margin: 0.5em 0.9em 0.4em 0em;=
">
<div class=3D"thumbinner mp-thumb" style=3D"background: transparent; color:=
 inherit; border: none; padding: 0; max-width: 125px;">
<span typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Maur=
ice_Suckling_by_Thomas_Bardwell.jpg" class=3D"mw-file-description" title=3D=
"Maurice Suckling"><img alt=3D"Maurice Suckling" src=3D"https://upload.wiki=
media.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Maurice_Suckling_by_Thomas_Bardwell.=
jpg/250px-Maurice_Suckling_by_Thomas_Bardwell.jpg" decoding=3D"async" width=
=3D"125" height=3D"158" class=3D"mw-file-element" data-file-width=3D"2400" =
data-file-height=3D"3030"></a></span></div></div>
<p><b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maurice_Suckling" title=3D"M=
aurice Suckling">Maurice Suckling</a></b> (4&#160;May 1726&#160;=E2=80=93 1=
4&#160;July 1778) was a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Navy=
" title=3D"Royal Navy">Royal Navy</a> officer and politician. He saw servic=
e in the English Channel and Mediterranean Sea during the <a href=3D"https:=
//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_of_the_Austrian_Succession" title=3D"War of the=
 Austrian Succession">War of the Austrian Succession</a>. At the start of t=
he <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven_Years%27_War" title=3D"Se=
ven Years' War">Seven Years' War</a>, he was promoted to captain and given =
a command on the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamaica_Station_(=
Royal_Navy)" title=3D"Jamaica Station (Royal Navy)">Jamaica Station</a>. Th=
ere he played a major part in the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/=
Battle_of_Cap-Fran%C3%A7ais" title=3D"Battle of Cap-Fran=C3=A7ais">Battle o=
f Cap-Fran=C3=A7ais</a>, and fought against the French ship <i><a href=3D"h=
ttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_ship_Palmier_(1752)" title=3D"French sh=
ip Palmier (1752)">Palmier</a></i>. Suckling was employed in the aftermath =
of the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capture_of_Belle_%C3%8Ele" =
title=3D"Capture of Belle =C3=8Ele">capture of Belle =C3=8Ele</a> to destro=
y French fortifications on the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3=
%8Ele-d%27Aix" title=3D"=C3=8Ele-d'Aix">=C3=8Ele-d'Aix</a> and went on <a h=
ref=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Half-pay" title=3D"Half-pay">half-pay<=
/a> at the end of the war. He was given his next command during the <a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Falklands_Crisis_of_1770" title=3D"Falkla=
nds Crisis of 1770">Falklands Crisis</a> in 1770, and took his nephew <a hr=
ef=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horatio_Nelson,_1st_Viscount_Nelson" ti=
tle=3D"Horatio Nelson, 1st Viscount Nelson">Horatio Nelson</a> with him. In=
 1775, Suckling was appointed as the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi=
ki/Comptroller_of_the_Navy_(Navy_Board)" title=3D"Comptroller of the Navy (=
Navy Board)">comptroller of the Navy</a> by <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia=
.org/wiki/John_Montagu,_4th_Earl_of_Sandwich" title=3D"John Montagu, 4th Ea=
rl of Sandwich">John Montagu, 4th Earl of Sandwich</a>, the <a href=3D"http=
s://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Lord_of_the_Admiralty" title=3D"First Lord =
of the Admiralty">first lord of the Admiralty</a>. Suckling oversaw the Roy=
al Navy's mobilisation when the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Am=
erican_Revolutionary_War" title=3D"American Revolutionary War">American Rev=
olutionary War</a> began. In 1776, he was also elected member of Parliament=
 for <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portsmouth_(UK_Parliament_con=
stituency)" title=3D"Portsmouth (UK Parliament constituency)">Portsmouth</a=
>. He died unexpectedly in 1778. <i>(<b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org=
/wiki/Maurice_Suckling" title=3D"Maurice Suckling">Full&#160;article...</a>=
</b>)</i>
</p>
