<p><b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truganini" title=3D"Truganin=
i">Truganini</a></b> (<abbr title=3D"circa">c.</abbr><span style=3D"white-s=
pace:nowrap;">=E2=80=891812</span> =E2=80=93 8 May 1876) was an <a href=3D"=
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aboriginal_Tasmanians" title=3D"Aboriginal Ta=
smanians">Aboriginal Tasmanian</a> woman of the <a href=3D"https://en.wikip=
edia.org/wiki/Nuenonne_language" title=3D"Nuenonne language">Nuenonne</a> p=
eople who was once widely described as the last surviving Aboriginal Tasman=
ian. She grew up on <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruny_Island" =
title=3D"Bruny Island">Bruny Island</a> and saw the death and displacement =
of much of Tasmania's Aboriginal population during the <a href=3D"https://e=
n.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_War" title=3D"Black War">Black War</a>. She acco=
mpanied <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Augustus_Robinson" =
title=3D"George Augustus Robinson">George Augustus Robinson</a> as a guide =
on expeditions that resulted in the exile of Tasmania's remaining Aborigina=
l population; Truganini herself was exiled to the <a href=3D"https://en.wik=
ipedia.org/wiki/Wybalenna_Aboriginal_Establishment" title=3D"Wybalenna Abor=
iginal Establishment">Wybalenna Aboriginal Establishment</a> after the expe=
ditions in 1835. She spent a period in the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.=
org/wiki/Port_Phillip_District" title=3D"Port Phillip District">Port Philli=
p District</a> (modern-day <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victori=
a_(state)" title=3D"Victoria (state)">Victoria</a>) where she was tried and=
 acquitted for involvement in the murder of two <a href=3D"https://en.wikip=
edia.org/wiki/Whaling_in_Australia" title=3D"Whaling in Australia">whalers<=
/a>. She was later moved to <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oyster=
_Cove,_Tasmania" title=3D"Oyster Cove, Tasmania">Oyster Cove</a>, where by =
1872 she was the only Aboriginal resident left and was mythologised as the =
last of her race. The narrative that Truganini was the last Aboriginal Tasm=
anian is rejected by scholars and by the contemporary Aboriginal Tasmanian =
community. She has become a symbol of what some have characterised as the <=
a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genocide_of_Indigenous_Australians"=
 title=3D"Genocide of Indigenous Australians">genocide of Indigenous Austra=
lians</a>. <i>(<b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truganini" title=
=3D"Truganini">Full&#160;article...</a></b>)</i>
</p>
