<p>The <b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan_Cup" title=3D"Japa=
n Cup">Japan Cup</a></b> is a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grou=
p_races" title=3D"Group races">Group 1 horse race</a> in Japan, held annual=
ly on the last Sunday of November at <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi=
ki/Tokyo_Racecourse" title=3D"Tokyo Racecourse">Tokyo Racecourse</a> in <a =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuch%C5%AB,_Tokyo" title=3D"Fuch=C5=
=AB, Tokyo">Fuch=C5=AB, Tokyo</a>. It is a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.=
org/wiki/Horse_racing#Flat_racing" title=3D"Horse racing">flat</a> race run=
 over a distance of 2400 metres (about <span class=3D"frac">1<span class=3D=
"sr-only">+</span><span class=3D"num">1</span>=E2=81=84<span class=3D"den">=
2</span></span> miles), with a maximum of 18 horses. First run in 1981, the=
 Japan Cup was created by the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japa=
n_Racing_Association" title=3D"Japan Racing Association">Japan Racing Assoc=
iation</a> and extends invitations to top-performing horses aged 3 and abov=
e from around the world. The race has had a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia=
.org/wiki/Purse_distribution" title=3D"Purse distribution">total prize purs=
e</a> of over one billion yen since 2023, and is the middle leg of the info=
rmal "<a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triple_Crown_of_Thoroughbred=
_Racing_(Japan)#Autumn_Triple_Crown" title=3D"Triple Crown of Thoroughbred =
Racing (Japan)">Autumn Triple Crown</a>" along with the <a href=3D"https://=
en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tenn%C5%8D_Sh%C5%8D_(Autumn)" title=3D"Tenn=C5=8D Sh=
=C5=8D (Autumn)">Tenn=C5=8D Sh=C5=8D (Autumn)</a> and the <a href=3D"https:=
//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arima_Kinen" title=3D"Arima Kinen">Arima Kinen</a>.=
 The Japan Cup is regularly ranked highly in the <a href=3D"https://en.wiki=
pedia.org/wiki/International_Federation_of_Horseracing_Authorities" title=
=3D"International Federation of Horseracing Authorities">International Fede=
ration of Horseracing Authorities</a>' "Top 100 Group 1 Races of the Year" =
compilation  due to the high quality and depth of racers, and has had winne=
rs from all over the world. Initially, the race was dominated by foreign ho=
rses, with 8 of the first 10 winners coming from abroad, however, in  the l=
ast twenty years only <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calandagan" =
title=3D"Calandagan">one horse</a> from outside Japan has won. <i>(<b><a hr=
ef=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan_Cup" title=3D"Japan Cup">Full&#16=
0;article...</a></b>)</i>
</p>
