<p>The <b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Bough_(Aeneid)" t=
itle=3D"Golden Bough (Aeneid)">Golden Bough</a></b> is a fantastical object=
 in the<i> <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aeneid" title=3D"Aeneid=
">Aeneid</a></i>, an <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epic_poetry" =
title=3D"Epic poetry">epic poem</a> by the 1st century BCE Roman poet <a hr=
ef=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virgil" title=3D"Virgil">Virgil</a>. Th=
e <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Troy" title=3D"Troy">Trojan</a> =
hero <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aeneas" title=3D"Aeneas">Aene=
as</a> is tasked to find the bough and remove it from its host tree to prov=
e his divine favour before his <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kat=
abasis" title=3D"Katabasis">journey into the Underworld</a>. It briefly res=
ists as he does so&#160;=E2=80=93 the implications of which have been widel=
y debated in scholarship. In the medieval period, commentators often interp=
reted the bough allegorically and as a symbol of wisdom. More recent schola=
rs have viewed the episode as reflecting Virgil's ambivalence towards the R=
oman Empire, and connected it to the deaths of two of Aeneas's antagonists,=
 <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dido" title=3D"Dido">Dido</a> and=
 <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turnus" title=3D"Turnus">Turnus</=
a>. The bough has been widely referenced in art and literature. It was used=
 by <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_George_Frazer" title=3D"=
James George Frazer">James Frazer</a> for the title of <a href=3D"https://e=
n.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Golden_Bough" title=3D"The Golden Bough">his 1890 =
work</a> on comparative religion, is recalled in <a href=3D"https://en.wiki=
pedia.org/wiki/Dante_Alighieri" title=3D"Dante Alighieri">Dante</a>'s <i><a=
 href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Divine_Comedy" title=3D"Divine Comed=
y">Divine Comedy</a></i>, and was the subject of <a href=3D"https://en.wiki=
pedia.org/wiki/The_Golden_Bough_(painting)" title=3D"The Golden Bough (pain=
ting)">an 1834 painting</a> by <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J._=
M._W._Turner" title=3D"J. M. W. Turner">J.&#160;M.&#160;W. Turner</a>. It i=
s also a recurring motif in the "Byzantium" poems of <a href=3D"https://en.=
wikipedia.org/wiki/W._B._Yeats" title=3D"W. B. Yeats">W.&#160;B. Yeats</a> =
and in the poetry of <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seamus_Heaney=
" title=3D"Seamus Heaney">Seamus Heaney</a>. <i>(<b><a href=3D"https://en.w=
ikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Bough_(Aeneid)" title=3D"Golden Bough (Aeneid)">Fu=
ll&#160;article...</a></b>)</i>
</p>
