<p><i><b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Splatoon_3:_Side_Order" t=
itle=3D"Splatoon 3: Side Order">Splatoon&#160;3: Side Order</a></b></i> is =
an <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expansion_pack" title=3D"Expans=
ion pack">expansion pack</a> for the single-player mode of <i><a href=3D"ht=
tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Splatoon_3" title=3D"Splatoon 3">Splatoon&#160;=
3</a></i> <i>(logo pictured)</i>, a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wik=
i/Video_game" title=3D"Video game">video game</a>. It was the second half o=
f the <i>Splatoon&#160;3 Expansion Pass</i> and was released on 22&#160;Feb=
ruary 2024. <i>Side Order</i> follows Agent&#160;8, who is  trapped in the =
featureless Memverse. They uncover Order, a rogue <a href=3D"https://en.wik=
ipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence" title=3D"Artificial intelligence">=
artificial intelligence</a> who threatens to abduct souls to remove their f=
ree will and make a world of complete order; Agent&#160;8 journeys up a thi=
rty-floor spire to destroy Order. Development began after the release of <i=
>Splatoon&#160;3</i> in 2022. The team sought to redo the traditional struc=
ture of <i>Splatoon</i> single-player campaigns, such as having the player'=
s death causing the loss of progress from their current climb, and the opti=
on to purchase upgrades to ease future attempts. <i>Side Order</i> received=
 favorable reviews, with praise given to its art direction and integration =
of <i>Splatoon</i><span class=3D"nowrap" style=3D"padding-left:0.1em;">'s</=
span> gameplay mechanics into the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/=
Roguelike" title=3D"Roguelike">roguelike</a> genre. Some critics disliked a=
 perceived lack of level diversity. <i>(<b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.=
org/wiki/Splatoon_3:_Side_Order" title=3D"Splatoon 3: Side Order">Full&#160=
;article...</a></b>)</i>
</p>
