<p>The <b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talyllyn_Railway" title=
=3D"Talyllyn Railway">Talyllyn Railway</a></b> is a <a href=3D"https://en.w=
ikipedia.org/wiki/Narrow-gauge_railway" title=3D"Narrow-gauge railway">narr=
ow-gauge</a> preserved railway in Wales running for 7.25 miles (11.67&#160;=
km) from <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tywyn" title=3D"Tywyn">Ty=
wyn</a> on the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mid_Wales" title=3D=
"Mid Wales">Mid Wales</a> coast to <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki=
/Nant_Gwernol_railway_station" title=3D"Nant Gwernol railway station">Nant =
Gwernol</a> near the village of <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ab=
ergynolwyn" title=3D"Abergynolwyn">Abergynolwyn</a>. The line was opened in=
 1866 to carry <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slate" title=3D"Sla=
te">slate</a> from the quarries at <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki=
/Bryn_Eglwys_quarry" title=3D"Bryn Eglwys quarry">Bryn Eglwys</a> to Tywyn,=
 and was the first narrow-gauge railway in Britain authorised by <a href=3D=
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Act_of_parliament#United_Kingdom" title=3D"A=
ct of parliament">act of Parliament</a> to carry passengers using steam hau=
lage. Despite severe under-investment, the line remained open, and on 14&#1=
60;May 1951 it became the first railway in the world to be operated as a <a=
 href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heritage_railway" title=3D"Heritage =
railway">heritage railway</a> by volunteers. Since preservation, the railwa=
y has operated as a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tourist_attrac=
tion" title=3D"Tourist attraction">tourist attraction</a>, significantly ex=
panding its rolling stock through acquisition and an engineering programme =
to build new locomotives and carriages. The fictional <a href=3D"https://en=
.wikipedia.org/wiki/Island_of_Sodor#Railways" title=3D"Island of Sodor">Ska=
rloey Railway</a>, which formed part of the <i><a href=3D"https://en.wikipe=
dia.org/wiki/The_Railway_Series" title=3D"The Railway Series">Railway Serie=
s</a></i> of children's books by the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi=
ki/Wilbert_Awdry" title=3D"Wilbert Awdry">Rev. W Awdry</a>, was based on th=
e Talyllyn Railway. The preservation of the line inspired the <a href=3D"ht=
tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ealing_comedies" title=3D"Ealing comedies">Eali=
ng comedy</a> film <i><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Titfield=
_Thunderbolt" title=3D"The Titfield Thunderbolt">The Titfield Thunderbolt</=
a></i>. <i>(<b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talyllyn_Railway" t=
itle=3D"Talyllyn Railway">Full&#160;article...</a></b>)</i>
</p>
