<p><b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Brevity" title=3D"=
Operation Brevity">Operation Brevity</a></b> was an offensive conducted in =
May&#160;1941, during the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_=
Desert_campaign" title=3D"Western Desert campaign">Western Desert campaign<=
/a> of the Second World War, against <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi=
ki/Axis_powers" title=3D"Axis powers">Axis</a> front-line forces in the <a =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sallum" title=3D"Sallum">Sollum</a>=
=E2=80=93<a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Capuzzo" title=3D"Fo=
rt Capuzzo">Capuzzo</a>=E2=80=93<a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ba=
rdia" title=3D"Bardia">Bardia</a> area of the border between Egypt and Liby=
a <i>(map pictured)</i>. British <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M=
iddle_East_Command" title=3D"Middle East Command">Middle East Command</a> g=
eneral <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archibald_Wavell,_1st_Earl_=
Wavell" title=3D"Archibald Wavell, 1st Earl Wavell">Archibald Wavell</a> de=
fined Operation Brevity's main goals as the acquisition of territory from w=
hich to launch a further planned offensive toward <a href=3D"https://en.wik=
ipedia.org/wiki/Tobruk" title=3D"Tobruk">Tobruk</a>. On 15&#160;May, Brigad=
ier <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Gott" title=3D"William=
 Gott">William Gott</a> attacked in three columns with a mixed infantry and=
 armoured force. The <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halfaya_Pass"=
 title=3D"Halfaya Pass">Halfaya Pass</a> was taken against stiff Italian op=
position, and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Capuzzo" title=
=3D"Fort Capuzzo">Fort Capuzzo</a> deeper inside Libya was captured, but Ge=
rman counter-attacks under Colonel <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki=
/Maximilian_von_Herff" title=3D"Maximilian von Herff">Maximilian von Herff<=
/a> regained the fort during the afternoon. Gott conducted a staged withdra=
wal to the Halfaya Pass on 16&#160;May, and Operation Brevity ended. The Ha=
lfaya Pass was recaptured 11 days later during <a href=3D"https://en.wikipe=
dia.org/wiki/Operation_Skorpion" title=3D"Operation Skorpion">Operation Sko=
rpion</a>, a German counter-attack. <i>(<b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.=
org/wiki/Operation_Brevity" title=3D"Operation Brevity">Full&#160;article..=
.</a></b>)</i>
</p>
