n" title=3D"Richard Harmon">Richard Harmon</a> <i>(pictured)</i>. Introduce=
d as a grandson of Iris Campbell, who escaped Death in the 1960s, Erik is r=
evealed to have been conceived out of his mother's affair and thus not in a=
ny danger. Despite this, while trying to help his brother cheat Death, Erik=
 is sucked into an <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnetic_resona=
nce_imaging" title=3D"Magnetic resonance imaging">MRI</a> machine by a whee=
lchair that crushes and impales him. The reveal of Erik's parentage was due=
 to the film's crew wanting to subvert the audience's expectations regardin=
g the order of deaths; a discarded idea involved twins. The directors were =
initially apprehensive about incorporating an MRI-machine death, but chose =
to include it due to positive feedback from the production team. Critics re=
sponded positively to Erik, describing him as a fan favorite and <i>Bloodli=
nes</i><span class=3D"nowrap" style=3D"padding-left:0.1em;">'</span> best c=
haracter, as well as praising his death scene and Harmon's performance. <i>=
(<b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erik_Campbell_(Final_Destinati=
on)" title=3D"Erik Campbell (Final Destination)">Full&#160;article...</a></=
b>)</i>
</p>
