></div></div>
<p>"<b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/All_Hell_Breaks_Loose_(Char=
med)" title=3D"All Hell Breaks Loose (Charmed)">All Hell Breaks Loose</a></=
b>" is the third-season finale of <i><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi=
ki/Charmed" title=3D"Charmed">Charmed</a></i>, an American <a href=3D"https=
://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fantasy" title=3D"Fantasy">fantasy</a> series that=
 aired on <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_WB" title=3D"The WB"=
>The WB</a>. It follows <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prue_Halli=
well" title=3D"Prue Halliwell">Prue</a> (<a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.or=
g/wiki/Shannen_Doherty" title=3D"Shannen Doherty">Shannen Doherty</a>), <a =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piper_Halliwell" title=3D"Piper Halli=
well">Piper</a> (<a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holly_Marie_Combs=
" title=3D"Holly Marie Combs">Holly Marie Combs</a>), and <a href=3D"https:=
//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phoebe_Halliwell" title=3D"Phoebe Halliwell">Phoebe=
 Halliwell</a> (<a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alyssa_Milano" tit=
le=3D"Alyssa Milano">Alyssa Milano</a>), three sisters who discover they ar=
e witches and use their powers to protect innocents from demons. "All Hell =
Breaks Loose" was written by <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brad_=
Kern" title=3D"Brad Kern">Brad Kern</a> and directed by Doherty <i>(picture=
d)</i>, and aired on May&#160;17, 2001. It was the third episode of the ser=
ies directed by Doherty. In the episode, Prue and Piper are caught using th=
eir powers on live television, which proves to have deadly consequences. Du=
ring filming, Doherty used a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salva=
dor_Dal%C3%AD" title=3D"Salvador Dal=C3=AD">Salvador Dal=C3=AD</a> painting=
 as inspiration for the episode's aesthetic, and helped her co-stars shoot =
emotionally challenging scenes. A week prior to the episode's airing, Doher=
ty was fired from the series due to a feud with Milano, which resulted in h=
er character being killed off. "All Hell Breaks Loose" has been cited as on=
e of the show's best episodes, with critics highlighting Prue's death. <i>(=
<b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/All_Hell_Breaks_Loose_(Charmed)=
" title=3D"All Hell Breaks Loose (Charmed)">Full&#160;article...</a></b>)</=
i>
</p>
