<p>The <b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silverthrone_Caldera" ti=
tle=3D"Silverthrone Caldera">Silverthrone Caldera</a></b> is a poorly studi=
ed volcano in the Range&#160;2 Coast Land District of <a href=3D"https://en=
.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Columbia" title=3D"British Columbia">British Co=
lumbia</a>, Canada. It lies within the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/=
wiki/Pacific_Ranges" title=3D"Pacific Ranges">Pacific Ranges</a> of the <a =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coast_Mountains" title=3D"Coast Mount=
ains">Coast Mountains</a> and reaches an elevation of 2,860 metres (9,380 f=
eet), although some sources give an elevation as high as 3,160&#160;m (10,3=
70&#160;ft). Deeply eroded, the caldera is about 25 by 20 kilometres (16 by=
 12 miles) in size and has a rugged topography. The area is the origin of s=
everal streams and contains several named <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.o=
rg/wiki/Mountain" title=3D"Mountain">mountains</a>, including <a href=3D"ht=
tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silverthrone_Mountain" title=3D"Silverthrone Mo=
untain">Silverthrone Mountain</a>. Volcanic rocks deposited by eruptions in=
clude <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhyolite" title=3D"Rhyolite"=
>rhyolites</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dacite" title=3D"D=
acite">dacites</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andesite" titl=
e=3D"Andesite">andesites</a> and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/B=
asaltic_andesite" title=3D"Basaltic andesite">basaltic andesites</a>. They =
are exposed in valleys, but at higher elevations they are largely buried un=
der glacial ice. The Silverthrone Caldera was a source of <a href=3D"https:=
//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Obsidian" title=3D"Obsidian">obsidian</a> for indig=
enous peoples during the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pre-Colum=
bian_era" title=3D"Pre-Columbian era">pre-Columbian era</a>. Geological stu=
dies have been conducted at the volcano since at least the 1960s, but its v=
ery remote location has impeded detailed fieldwork. <i>(<b><a href=3D"https=
://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silverthrone_Caldera" title=3D"Silverthrone Calder=
a">Full&#160;article...</a></b>)</i>
</p>
