=3D"Battles of Saratoga">at Saratoga</a></div></div></div>
<p>The <b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maryland_and_Virginia_Ri=
fle_Regiment" title=3D"Maryland and Virginia Rifle Regiment">Maryland and V=
irginia Rifle Regiment</a></b> was organized in June&#160;1776 as a <a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light_infantry" title=3D"Light infantry">=
light infantry</a> unit of riflemen in the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.=
org/wiki/Continental_Army" title=3D"Continental Army">Continental Army</a> =
during the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Revolutionary_=
War" title=3D"American Revolutionary War">American Revolutionary War</a>. T=
he <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regiment" title=3D"Regiment">re=
giment</a> consisted of nine <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compa=
ny_(military_unit)" title=3D"Company (military unit)">companies</a>&#160;=
=E2=80=93 four from Maryland and five from Virginia&#160;=E2=80=93 and was =
directly responsible to national authority as an <a href=3D"https://en.wiki=
pedia.org/wiki/Extra_Continental_regiments_and_Additional_Continental_regim=
ents" title=3D"Extra Continental regiments and Additional Continental regim=
ents">Extra Continental regiment</a>. Most of the regiment surrendered to B=
ritish and German forces at the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ba=
ttle_of_Fort_Washington" title=3D"Battle of Fort Washington">Battle of Fort=
 Washington</a> on November&#160;16, 1776. However, a portion of the unit c=
ontinued to serve actively in the Continental Army throughout most of the r=
emainder of the war. Elements of the regiment served with <a href=3D"https:=
//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Washington" title=3D"George Washington">Geor=
ge Washington</a>'s main army and participated in its major engagements. Se=
lect members of the unit were also attached to Colonel <a href=3D"https://e=
n.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daniel_Morgan" title=3D"Daniel Morgan">Daniel Morgan</=
a>'s elite <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morgan%27s_Riflemen" ti=
tle=3D"Morgan's Riflemen">Provisional Rifle Corps</a>. The regiment was reo=
rganized in January&#160;1779 and stationed at <a href=3D"https://en.wikipe=
dia.org/wiki/Fort_Pitt_(Pennsylvania)" title=3D"Fort Pitt (Pennsylvania)">F=
ort Pitt</a>, headquarters of the Continental Army's <a href=3D"https://en.=
wikipedia.org/wiki/Departments_of_the_Continental_Army" title=3D"Department=
s of the Continental Army">Western Department</a>, in present-day western <=
a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pennsylvania" title=3D"Pennsylvania=
">Pennsylvania</a>. Disbanded in January&#160;1781, it was the longest serv=
ing Continental Army rifle unit of the war. <i>(<b><a href=3D"https://en.wi=
kipedia.org/wiki/Maryland_and_Virginia_Rifle_Regiment" title=3D"Maryland an=
d Virginia Rifle Regiment">Full&#160;article...</a></b>)</i>
</p>
