=3D"1152" data-file-height=3D"864"></a></span></div></div>
<p>The <b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2006_Football_League_Cha=
mpionship_play-off_final" title=3D"2006 Football League Championship play-o=
ff final">2006 Football League Championship play-off final</a></b> was an <=
a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Association_football" title=3D"Asso=
ciation football">association football</a> match played on 21&#160;May 2006=
 at the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millennium_Stadium" title=
=3D"Millennium Stadium">Millennium Stadium</a> in <a href=3D"https://en.wik=
ipedia.org/wiki/Cardiff" title=3D"Cardiff">Cardiff</a>, Wales, between <a h=
ref=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leeds_United_F.C." title=3D"Leeds Unit=
ed F.C.">Leeds United</a> and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watf=
ord_F.C." title=3D"Watford F.C.">Watford</a>. The match was to determine th=
e third and final team to gain <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pro=
motion_and_relegation" title=3D"Promotion and relegation">promotion</a> fro=
m the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/EFL_Championship" title=3D"E=
FL Championship">Football League Championship</a>, the second tier of <a hr=
ef=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_football_league_system" title=
=3D"English football league system">English football</a>, to the <a href=3D=
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Premier_League" title=3D"Premier League">FA =
Premiership</a>. The winners of two semi-finals competed for the final Prem=
iership place of the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2006%E2%80%93=
07_FA_Premier_League" title=3D"2006=E2=80=9307 FA Premier League"><span cla=
ss=3D"nowrap">2006=E2=80=9307</span> season</a>. Winning the final was esti=
mated to be worth up to =C2=A340&#160;million to the successful team. The m=
atch was watched by a crowd of 64,736. It was the last <a href=3D"https://e=
n.wikipedia.org/wiki/EFL_Championship_play-offs" title=3D"EFL Championship =
play-offs">play-off</a> final to be held at the Millennium Stadium, as the =
new <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wembley_Stadium" title=3D"Wemb=
ley Stadium">Wembley Stadium</a> was completed in time for the <a href=3D"h=
ttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2007_Football_League_Championship_play-off_fin=
al" title=3D"2007 Football League Championship play-off final">2007 final</=
a>. Watford won the match <span class=3D"nowrap">3=E2=80=930</span>, with o=
pening goalscorer <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jay_DeMerit" tit=
le=3D"Jay DeMerit">Jay DeMerit</a> named <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.or=
g/wiki/Player_of_the_match" title=3D"Player of the match">man of the match<=
/a>. Leeds goalkeeper <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neil_Sulliva=
n" title=3D"Neil Sullivan">Neil Sullivan</a> scored an <a href=3D"https://e=
n.wikipedia.org/wiki/Own_goal" title=3D"Own goal">own goal</a> to make the =
score <span class=3D"nowrap">2=E2=80=930</span> to Watford after 60 minutes=
, and the final goal was a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penalty=
_kick_(association_football)" title=3D"Penalty kick (association football)"=
>penalty kick</a> scored by <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darius=
_Henderson" title=3D"Darius Henderson">Darius Henderson</a>. <i>(<b><a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2006_Football_League_Championship_play-of=
f_final" title=3D"2006 Football League Championship play-off final">Full&#1=
60;article...</a></b>)</i>
</p>
