of a male <i>Intraproboscis sanghae</i></div></div></div>
<p><i><b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intraproboscis" title=3D"=
Intraproboscis">Intraproboscis</a></b></i> is a genus in <a href=3D"https:/=
/en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acanthocephala" title=3D"Acanthocephala">Acanthoceph=
ala</a> (thorny-headed or spiny-headed <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/=
wiki/Parasitism" title=3D"Parasitism">parasitic</a> worms) containing a sin=
gle species. Found in Central Africa, it infests the <a href=3D"https://en.=
wikipedia.org/wiki/Long-tailed_pangolin" title=3D"Long-tailed pangolin">bla=
ck-bellied pangolin</a> and the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wh=
ite-bellied_pangolin" title=3D"White-bellied pangolin">tree pangolin</a>, w=
hich are both threatened with <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exti=
nction" title=3D"Extinction">extinction</a>. Female worms reach up to 180&#=
160;mm (7.1&#160;in) long (mostly <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/=
Torso" title=3D"Torso">trunk</a>) and 2&#160;mm (0.079&#160;in) wide; males=
 seem to be smaller. The body consists of a long, narrow trunk and a tubula=
r <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proboscis" title=3D"Proboscis">p=
roboscis</a> covered with hooks <i>(pictured)</i>, used for feeding and att=
achment. The life cycle of <i>I.&#160;sanghae</i> remains unknown but it li=
kely involves a complex <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biological=
_life_cycle" title=3D"Biological life cycle">life cycle</a> with at least t=
wo hosts, the pangolin and one believed to be an <a href=3D"https://en.wiki=
pedia.org/wiki/Arthropod" title=3D"Arthropod">arthropod</a>, such as an ins=
ect. Within this host, the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Larva" =
title=3D"Larva">larvae</a> develop into an infectious stage called a cystac=
anth. When a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vertebrate" title=3D"=
Vertebrate">vertebrate</a> consumes the intermediate host, the cystacanths =
enter the intestines where they mature. The worm's eggs are expelled and ha=
tch into new larvae. Infestation by <i>I.&#160;sanghae</i> can cause <a hre=
f=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gastrointestinal_perforation" title=3D"G=
astrointestinal perforation">intestinal perforation</a> and death in the bl=
ack-bellied pangolin. <i>(<b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intra=
proboscis" title=3D"Intraproboscis">Full&#160;article...</a></b>)</i>
