 href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capital_Indoor_Stadium" title=3D"Cap=
ital Indoor Stadium">Capital Indoor Stadium</a> <i>(pictured)</i> in <a hre=
f=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beijing" title=3D"Beijing">Beijing</a>, =
China. It consisted of competitions in <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/=
wiki/Single_skating" title=3D"Single skating">men's singles, women's single=
s</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pair_skating" title=3D"Pair=
 skating">pair skating</a>, and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ic=
e_dance" title=3D"Ice dance">ice dance</a>. Skaters and teams earned points=
 based on their placements in each event; medalists were determined based o=
n their total points. The team representing the <a href=3D"https://en.wikip=
edia.org/wiki/Russian_Olympic_Committee" title=3D"Russian Olympic Committee=
">Russian Olympic Committee</a> originally finished in first place, while t=
he team from the United States finished second, and the Japanese team third=
. The medal ceremony was postponed when a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.o=
rg/wiki/Doping_in_sport" title=3D"Doping in sport">positive test confirming=
