<p><b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sally_Ride" title=3D"Sally R=
ide">Sally Ride</a></b> (May&#160;26, 1951&#160;=E2=80=93 July&#160;23, 201=
2) was an American astronaut and physicist. Born in Los Angeles, she joined=
 <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NASA" title=3D"NASA">NASA</a> in =
1978, and in 1983 became the third woman and the first American woman to fl=
y in space. A graduate of <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanford=
_University" title=3D"Stanford University">Stanford University</a>, where s=
he earned a PhD in physics in 1978, she was selected as a <a href=3D"https:=
//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mission_specialist" title=3D"Mission specialist">mi=
ssion specialist</a> with <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NASA_Ast=
ronaut_Group_8" title=3D"NASA Astronaut Group 8">NASA Astronaut Group&#160;=
8</a>, the first class of NASA astronauts to include women. She flew in spa=
ce on the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Shuttle_Challenger=
" title=3D"Space Shuttle Challenger">Space Shuttle <i>Challenger</i></a> on=
 the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/STS-7" title=3D"STS-7"><span =
class=3D"nowrap">STS-7</span></a> mission in 1983 and the <a href=3D"https:=
//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/STS-41-G" title=3D"STS-41-G"><span class=3D"nowrap"=
>STS-41-G</span></a> mission in 1984.  She left NASA in 1987 and worked at =
Stanford's <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanford_University_cen=
ters_and_institutes#Freeman_Spogli_Institute_for_International_Studies" tit=
le=3D"Stanford University centers and institutes">Center for International =
Security and Arms Control</a>, and then at the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipe=
dia.org/wiki/University_of_California,_San_Diego" title=3D"University of Ca=
lifornia, San Diego">University of California, San Diego</a>, researching <=
a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nonlinear_optics" title=3D"Nonlinea=
r optics">nonlinear optics</a> and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki=
/Thomson_scattering" title=3D"Thomson scattering">Thomson scattering</a>. S=
he served on the committees that investigated the <a href=3D"https://en.wik=
ipedia.org/wiki/Space_Shuttle_Challenger_disaster" title=3D"Space Shuttle C=
hallenger disaster">losses of <i>Challenger</i></a> and <a href=3D"https://=
en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Shuttle_Columbia_disaster" title=3D"Space Shutt=
le Columbia disaster">of <i>Columbia</i></a>, and was the only person to pa=
rticipate in both investigations. She is the first astronaut known to have =
been LGBTQ, a fact that she hid until her death from <a href=3D"https://en.=
wikipedia.org/wiki/Pancreatic_cancer" title=3D"Pancreatic cancer">pancreati=
c cancer</a> in 2012. <i>(<b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sally=
_Ride" title=3D"Sally Ride">Full&#160;article...</a></b>)</i>
</p>
