<p>The <b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nation_of_Islam" title=
=3D"Nation of Islam">Nation of Islam</a></b> (NOI) is a religious organizat=
ion founded in the United States by <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wik=
i/Wallace_Fard_Muhammad" title=3D"Wallace Fard Muhammad">Wallace Fard Muham=
mad</a> in 1930. It is centralized, hierarchical, and committed to <a href=
=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_nationalism" title=3D"Black nationa=
lism">black nationalism</a>; membership is open only to <a href=3D"https://=
en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Person_of_color" title=3D"Person of color">people of =
color</a>. Practitioners are expected to live disciplined lives, adhering t=
o patriarchal gender roles, strict dress codes and specific dietary require=
ments. The NOI campaigns for the creation of an independent <a href=3D"http=
s://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_Americans" title=3D"African Americans">Af=
rican-American</a> nation-state and calls for African Americans to be econo=
mically self-sufficient. In 2007, it was estimated to have 50,000 members. =
While describing itself as Islamic and using Islamic terminology, its relig=
ious tenets differ substantially from orthodox <a href=3D"https://en.wikipe=
dia.org/wiki/Islamic_schools_and_branches" title=3D"Islamic schools and bra=
nches">Islamic traditions</a>. <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rel=
igious_studies" title=3D"Religious studies">Scholars of religion</a> charac=
terize it as a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_religious_movem=
ent" title=3D"New religious movement">new religious movement</a>. Muslim cr=
itics accuse the NOI of promoting teachings that are not authentically Isla=
mic. Other critics have characterized it as a <a href=3D"https://en.wikiped=
ia.org/wiki/Hate_group" title=3D"Hate group">hate group</a> that <a href=3D=
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nation_of_Islam_and_antisemitism" title=3D"N=
ation of Islam and antisemitism">promotes antisemitism</a>, <a href=3D"http=
s://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anti-White_racism" title=3D"Anti-White racism">ra=
cism against white people</a>, and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki=
/Anti-LGBTQ_rhetoric" title=3D"Anti-LGBTQ rhetoric">anti-LGBTQ rhetoric</a>=
. <i>(<b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nation_of_Islam" title=3D=
"Nation of Islam">Full&#160;article...</a></b>)</i>
</p>
