<div class=3D"thumbinner mp-thumb" style=3D"background: transparent; color:=
 inherit; border: none; padding: 0; max-width: 127px;">
<span typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Patr=
ick_henry.JPG" class=3D"mw-file-description" title=3D"Patrick Henry"><img a=
lt=3D"Patrick Henry" src=3D"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/=
thumb/e/ea/Patrick_henry.JPG/250px-Patrick_henry.JPG" decoding=3D"async" wi=
dth=3D"127" height=3D"153" class=3D"mw-file-element" data-file-width=3D"610=
" data-file-height=3D"737"></a></span></div></div>
<p><b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrick_Henry" title=3D"Patr=
ick Henry">Patrick Henry</a></b> (May&#160;29, 1736&#160;=E2=80=93 June&#16=
0;6, 1799) was an American attorney known for his declaration to the <a hre=
f=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virginia_Conventions" title=3D"Virginia =
Conventions">Second Virginia Convention</a> in 1775: "<a href=3D"https://en=
.wikipedia.org/wiki/Give_me_liberty_or_give_me_death!" title=3D"Give me lib=
erty or give me death!">Give me liberty or give me death!</a>"  Beginning a=
 law practice in 1760, he soon became prominent through his victory in the =
<a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parson%27s_Cause" title=3D"Parson'=
s Cause">Parson's Cause</a>. Henry was elected to the Virginia <a href=3D"h=
ttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Burgesses" title=3D"House of Burgesse=
s">House of Burgesses</a>, where he quickly became notable for his inflamma=
tory rhetoric against the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stamp_Ac=
t_1765" title=3D"Stamp Act 1765">Stamp Act of 1765</a>. In 1774 and 1775, H=
enry served as a delegate to the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F=
irst_Continental_Congress" title=3D"First Continental Congress">First</a> a=
nd <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Continental_Congress" ti=
tle=3D"Second Continental Congress">Second Continental Congresses</a>. Back=
 in <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virginia" title=3D"Virginia">V=
irginia</a>, Henry urged independence, and when this was declared, served a=
s <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Governor_of_Virginia" title=3D"G=
overnor of Virginia">governor</a> until 1779, and then in the <a href=3D"ht=
tps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virginia_House_of_Delegates" title=3D"Virginia =
House of Delegates">Virginia House of Delegates</a> until he began his last=
 two terms as governor in 1784. Henry feared a strong federal government, a=
nd he actively opposed the ratification of the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipe=
dia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_the_United_States" title=3D"Constitution of th=
e United States">U.S. Constitution</a>. A slaveholder throughout his adult =
life, he hoped to see slavery end, but had no plan to accomplish that. Henr=
y is remembered for his oratory, and as a <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.o=
rg/wiki/Founding_Fathers_of_the_United_States" title=3D"Founding Fathers of=
 the United States">Founding Father</a>. <i>(<b><a href=3D"https://en.wikip=
edia.org/wiki/Patrick_Henry" title=3D"Patrick Henry">Full&#160;article...</=
a></b>)</i>
</p>
