<span typeof=3D"mw:File"><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Bice=
ntenial_Capitol_Mall_Park.jpg" class=3D"mw-file-description" title=3D"Bicen=
tennial Capitol Mall State Park"><img alt=3D"Bicentennial Capitol Mall Stat=
e Park" src=3D"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Bi=
centenial_Capitol_Mall_Park.jpg/250px-Bicentenial_Capitol_Mall_Park.jpg" de=
coding=3D"async" width=3D"171" height=3D"114" class=3D"mw-file-element" dat=
a-file-width=3D"2250" data-file-height=3D"1500"></a></span></div></div>
<p>The <b><a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bicentennial_Capitol_Mal=
l_State_Park" title=3D"Bicentennial Capitol Mall State Park">Bicentennial C=
apitol Mall State Park</a></b> is an urban <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.=
org/wiki/Linear_park" title=3D"Linear park">linear park</a> in downtown <a =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nashville,_Tennessee" title=3D"Nashvi=
lle, Tennessee">Nashville, Tennessee</a>, United States. The park is 19 acr=
es (7.7 hectares) in size and adjoins the grounds of the <a href=3D"https:/=
/en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tennessee_State_Capitol" title=3D"Tennessee State Ca=
pitol">Tennessee State Capitol</a>. It is modeled on the <a href=3D"https:/=
/en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Mall" title=3D"National Mall">National Mall=
</a> in <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington,_D.C." title=3D=
"Washington, D.C.">Washington, D.C.</a>, and incorporates <a href=3D"https:=
//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Greek_architecture" title=3D"Ancient Greek =
architecture">Classical Greek</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki=
/Baroque_architecture" title=3D"Baroque architecture">Baroque</a>, and <a h=
ref=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beaux-Arts_architecture" title=3D"Beau=
x-Arts architecture">Beaux-Arts architecture</a>. It uses <a href=3D"https:=
//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artistic_symbol" title=3D"Artistic symbol">symbolis=
m</a> to showcase the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_T=
ennessee" title=3D"History of Tennessee">history</a>, <a href=3D"https://en=
.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geography_of_Tennessee" title=3D"Geography of Tennessee=
">geography</a>, <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tennessee#culture=
" title=3D"Tennessee">culture</a>, and <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/=
wiki/Music_of_Tennessee" title=3D"Music of Tennessee">musical heritage of T=
ennessee</a> through a series of monuments, walkways, and interpretive disp=
lays. Receiving more than 2.5&#160;million visitors annually, it is the mos=
t visited of the 57 <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Tennes=
see_state_parks_and_natural_areas" title=3D"List of Tennessee state parks a=
nd natural areas">state parks in Tennessee</a>. The park was designed by Tu=
ck Hinton Architects in 1992 and 1993, groundbreaking occurred on June&#160=
;27, 1994, and the park was dedicated on June&#160;1, 1996, the 200th anniv=
ersary of <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tennessee" title=3D"Tenn=
essee">Tennessee</a>'s statehood. Since then, the <a href=3D"https://en.wik=
ipedia.org/wiki/Tennessee_State_Museum" title=3D"Tennessee State Museum">Te=
nnessee State Museum</a> and the <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T=
ennessee_State_Library_and_Archives" title=3D"Tennessee State Library and A=
rchives">Tennessee State Library and Archives</a> have moved to the park, w=
hich is now recognized as a cultural and historical landmark. <i>(<b><a hre=
f=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bicentennial_Capitol_Mall_State_Park" ti=
tle=3D"Bicentennial Capitol Mall State Park">Full&#160;article...</a></b>)<=
/i>
</p>
